results.problem:
Let \( f \) be a function defined on the set of non-negative real numbers and taking values therein. Find all \( f \) that satisfy the following conditions:
1. \( f(x f(y)) f(y) = f(x + y) \);
2. \( f(2) = 0 \);
3. \( f(x) \neq 0 \) for \( 0 \leq x < 2 \).

On the side \(A_{1} A_{2}\) of a regular \(n\)-gon \(A_{1} A_{2} A_{3} \ldots A_{n}\), point \(M_{1}\) is chosen. This point is projected from vertex \(A_{n}\) to point \(M_{2}\) on side \(A_{2} A_{3}\) or its extension (i.e., \(M_{2}\) is the intersection of line \(A_{n} M_{1}\) with line \(A_{2} A_{3}\)); then point \(M_{2}\) is projected from vertex \(A_{1}\) to point \(M_{3}\) on side \(A_{3} A_{4}\); point \(M_{3}\) is projected from vertex \(A_{2}\) to point \(M_{4}\) on side \(A_{4} A_{5}\), and so on. This process does not stop after one traversal of all the sides of the \(n\)-gon but continues indefinitely. Prove that:

a) If \(n=4\), then the point \(M_{13}\) on side \(A_{1} A_{2}\), which is obtained after three rounds of all sides of the polygon, coincides with \(M_{1}\) (and therefore, \(M_{14}\) coincides with \(M_{2}\), \(M_{15}\) coincides with \(M_{3}\), etc.);

b) If \(n=6\), then the point \(M_{13}\) on side \(A_{1} A_{2}\), which is obtained after two rounds of all sides of the polygon, coincides with \(M_{1}\) (and therefore, \(M_{14}\) coincides with \(M_{2}\), \(M_{15}\) coincides with \(M_{3}\), etc.);

c) If \(n=10\), then the point \(M_{11}\) on side \(A_{1} A_{2}\), which is obtained after one round of all sides of the polygon, coincides with \(M_{1}\) (and therefore, \(M_{12}\) coincides with \(M_{2}\), \(M_{13}\) coincides with \(M_{3}\), etc.).

Note: It can be proved that if \(n\) is different from 4, 6, and 10, none of the points \(M_{kn+1}\), \(k=1,2,3,\ldots\), obtained in the described manner on side \(A_{1} A_{2}\), will coincide with the initial point \(M_{2}\). Thus, the process will continue indefinitely without the points beginning to repeat.

Calculate the value of the function:

1) \( f(x) = \sqrt{x^2 - 5x + 4} \)

   a) when \( x = 0 \); b) when \( x = a + 1 \);

2) \( \varphi(x) = 2 \arcsin x + \operatorname{arctg} 2x \) when \( x = -\frac{1}{2} \);

3) \( y = x^2 \arccos \frac{x}{2} - 3x \operatorname{arcctg} x \) when \( x = -1 \).

results.ground_truth:
\begin{aligned}
&\text{The lengths of the catheti } a \text{ and } b \text{ are given by } 2mn \text{ and } m^2 - n^2, \\ 
&\text{and the hypotenuse } c \text{ is given by } m^2 + n^2, \text{ where } m \text{ and } n \text{ are natural numbers.}
\end{aligned}

